    startingPosition: "Seated facing side.\nPelvis and spine neutral.\nKnees flexed, leg furthest from the bar internally rotated, leg closest to the bar laterally rotated with the foot against the opposite knee.\nPelvis square and as level as possible (may sit on one cheek).\nClosest arm long, holding the bar just in front of the shoulder, palm down\nOther arm relaxed at the side, palm up.\nScapulae stabilized.",
    pelvis: "Held stable while the spine laterally flexes and rotates toward the bar, then returns to vertical and lengthens forward into a lean",
    spine: "Elbow of the bar arm flexes to begin pulling the bar down while the gesture arm reaches overhead\nThe arm extends to push the bar down and through the uprights as the pelvis stays stable and the spine laterally flexes toward the bar, then rotates so the upper torso faces the bar with both hands taking it shoulder-distance apart\nBoth elbows flex/extend three times in this rotated, laterally-flexed position\nThen, maintaining rotation, the spine sequentially lengthens to vertical from the tail while elbows flex bringing the bar toward the chest, before the arms lengthen upward and the whole torso leans forward as one line, reaching the crown toward the bar",
    breathing: "Inhale to flex the elbow of the bar arm, beginning to pull it down, while reaching the gesture arm overhead\nExhale to extend the arm, pushing the bar down and through the uprights, while laterally flexing the spine toward the bar, then rotating the upper torso to face the bar, both hands taking it shoulder-distance apart\nInhale, pelvis stable and spine in flexion/rotation, to flex both elbows bringing the bar toward the head\nExhale to extend the elbows — repeat the flex/extend three times\nThen inhale, maintaining the torso rotation, to initiate from the tail and sequentially lengthen the spine to vertical while flexing the elbows to bring the bar toward the chest\nExhale to lengthen the arms upward and lean the whole torso — pelvis, spine, and head as one line — forward with abdominal support, reaching the crown toward the bar\nContinues through a mirrored sequence (hinge to vertical, flex forward, rotate the other way, laterally flex away, return) to complete the full pattern.\n2 reps each side.",
    targetMuscles: "Transversus abdominis and pelvic floor\nInternal/external obliques of the side closest to the bar concentrically to laterally flex the torso\nExternal oblique on one side and internal oblique on the other concentrically to rotate the upper torso toward the bar\nRectus abdominis/obliques concentrically to flex the spine\nTop-side internal/external obliques concentrically to return to vertical\nObliques to prevent lumbar overextension during the lean\nScapular stabilizers",
    focus: "Maintain neutral spine alignment, avoiding the rib cage lifting or pushing forward\nStabilize scapulae on both the gesture-arm and supporting-arm sides\nLengthen the spine before laterally flexing to avoid crunching into the side\nMaintain control of the bar, partially supporting body weight with the lats\nKeep the furthest hip still as the spine laterally flexes and rotates\nSupport with abdominals when leaning the torso to avoid extending the spine\nMake sure to pass through the sidebend position on the return",
