    focus: "This helps increase flexibility further.\nMaintain the cervical spine in line with the thoracic spine — do not allow the weight of the head to hang back and extend the neck\nOnly extend the legs as far as parallel alignment can be maintained through hips, knees and ankles\nAvoid overextending the knees, especially as the ankles dorsiflex\nSupport the torso with core muscles so the shoulders can remain stabilized without being overstretched",
